# Site image chrome

Every **generated** raster image on this site (insight heroes, call images, infographics, diagram PNGs via GenerateImage) must include both of these, and nothing else as brand copy.

| Slot | Put | Do not put |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Top left** | G.A.I.N **mark**: white circle with hex wireframe icon + wordmark **G.A.I.N** | Slogan under the logo. No TRUST / CONTROL / IMPACT. No G.A.I.N SYSTEMS unless the canvas is wide and the navbar lockup is the brief. |
| **Bottom right** | Source URL **jitendersharma.dev** in small, readable sans-serif | **gain.inc** or any other domain. That URL is a different company. |

The diagram, title, and footer claims (e.g. "Governed. Observable. Secure.") are content. The mark and URL are chrome. Do not invent a three-word tagline.

**Compose in GenerateImage.** Chrome must be **composed in the original GenerateImage**, not stamped afterwards. When generating, reserve empty padding in the top-left and bottom-right (no title, no diagram labels, no legend in those corners). NEVER overlay or composite a logo or URL onto an existing PNG that already has content in those corners. NEVER use `scripts/restamp-site-image-chrome.py` for new images.

**Out of scope:** mermaid, author photos, vendor/credential logos, screenshots of the live UI.

When calling **GenerateImage**, put both chrome items in the `description` every time. Match `static/img/logo.svg` for the icon (circle + hex wireframe + center dot). Tell the model to leave clear empty space in those corners for the mark and URL.
